# scikit-robot from its git main branch: this package
# subclasses actuo_ros' RobotInterface, which subclasses skrobot's ros2
# interface. Two different scikit-robots would be two different base classes.
scikit-robot @ git+https://github.com/iory/scikit-robot.git@main

# The interactive shell. Falls back to `code.interact` if absent, but the
# history and completion are the point.
ipython

numpy

# Geometry for actuo.safety's SelfCollisionMonitor (fcl), with the SAME
# scikit-robot as the shell.
python-fcl

# Image processing for the camera exercises (track_box). The ROS-side cv2
# (python3-opencv) is built against NumPy 1 and does not import next to this
# venv's NumPy 2, and cv_bridge rides on it; so the wheel, and ri.image()
# decodes sensor_msgs/Image itself.
opencv-python-headless
# Showing camera images (show_camera, and students' own programs). The apt
# python3-matplotlib is built against NumPy 1 and fails to import next to this
# venv's NumPy 2 ("numpy.core.multiarray failed to import"), so the wheel.
# Its window needs tkinter, which is the system's python3-tk (package.xml).
matplotlib

# shapely in this venv, not from the system. trimesh (via scikit-robot) imports
# it when present, and with --system-site-packages an apt python3-shapely
# (pulled in by e.g. ROS One jsk_recognition_utils) is found instead: built for
# NumPy 1, it prints "A module that was compiled using NumPy 1.x cannot be run
# in NumPy 2" on every start. PyPI shapely 2.x is built for NumPy 2.
shapely
